error[E0277]: `Option<i64>` may lower to `Value::Null`, so it cannot go inside an `Option`
 --> tests/ui/nested_option.rs:7:12
  |
7 |     maybe: Option<Option<i64>>,
  |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `Option<Option<i64>>` would collapse `Some(null)` and `None` into one value
  |
  = help: the trait `NotNullable` is not implemented for `Option<i64>`
  = note: Nested options have no representation in the store: flatten `Option<Option<T>>` to `Option<T>`.
          A `duet_core::Value` can already be `Value::Null`, so an `Option` around one is the same collapse.
          For a type of your own, add an empty `impl NotNullable for Option<i64>` next to its `SharedState` impl.
  = help: the following other types implement trait `NotNullable`:
            App
            Arc<T>
            BTreeMap<String, V>
            Box<T>
            HashMap<String, V, S>
            String
            Vec<T>
            bool
          and $N others
  = note: required for `Option<Option<i64>>` to implement `SharedState`
